  "summary": "JetBrains Exposed: SQL injection via unescaped string arguments of SQL functions",
  "details": "In JetBrains Exposed before 1.5.1 SQL injection was possible via unescaped string arguments of several SQL functions.\n\nThe string arguments of `locate()`, `concat()`, `groupConcat()`, `match()` and of the JSON functions `extract()`, `exists()` and `contains()` were written into the SQL statement instead of being bound as query parameters. Version 1.5.1 binds them as parameters (EXPOSED-1093).",
